0,Dogon people - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dogon_people,"The Dogon are an ethnic group indigenous to the central plateau region of Mali, in West Africa, south of the Niger bend, near the city of Bandiagara, and in Burkina Faso. The population numbers between 400,000 and 800,000. [3] They speak the Dogon languages, which are considered to constitute an independent branch of the Niger–Congo language family, meaning that they are not closely related ...","Dogon, Togo Kan",Niger-Congo
1,Dogon languages - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dogon_languages,"The Dogon languages are a small closely related language family that is spoken by the Dogon people of Mali and may belong to the proposed Niger–Congo family. There are about 600,000 speakers of its dozen languages.","Dogon, Togo Kan",Niger-Congo
